		\midrule
		Full Audio-Agent         & \textbf{21.86} & All components            \\
		- Text modality          & 23.45          & Audio-only retrieval      \\
		- Audio modality         & 35.67          & Text-only retrieval       \\
		- TRR (use mean pooling) & 24.89          & Standard vector retrieval \\
		- Uncertainty weighting  & 22.34          & Fixed 50/50 weights       \\
		- Constraint repair      & 23.12          & No constraint enforcement \\
		\bottomrule
	\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\section{Implementation Details}

\subsection{WebSocket Communication Protocol}

The WebSocket communication between Python agent and C++ client uses a JSON-based message format.

\textbf{Message Format}:
\begin{verbatim}
{
  "type": "parameter_update",
  "timestamp": 1234567890.123,
  "parameters": {
    "eq_low_gain": 2.5,
    "eq_mid_freq": 1200.0,
    "comp_threshold": -18.5,
    "comp_ratio": 4.3,
    ...
  },
  "metadata": {
    "query": "warm vintage breakup",
    "retrieved_presets": ["Tweed Clean", "British Crunch"],
    "confidence": 0.87
  }
}
\end{verbatim}

\textbf{Acknowledgment Format}:
\begin{verbatim}
{
  "type": "ack",
  "status": "success" | "error",
  "message": "Parameters applied successfully" | "Invalid range for comp_ratio",
  "applied_parameters": {...}
}
\end{verbatim}

\subsection{Performance Optimization}

\textbf{Caching Strategy}. We cache TRR embeddings for all database items to enable fast retrieval. The cache is stored as a memory-mapped numpy array for efficient random access.

\textbf{Parallelization}. Text and audio retrieval are performed in parallel using Python's multiprocessing module. This reduces query latency by approximately 40\%.

\textbf{Batch Processing}. For batch inference, we process multiple queries simultaneously using vectorized operations, improving throughput by 3-4x compared to sequential processing.

